  ('economics/firms-and-market-structures/the-firm-and-market-structures', 'economics', 'economics/firms-and-market-structures', 'The Firm and Market Structures', 'the-firm-and-market-structures', 'How a firm''s costs shape its output decisions, and how a market''s structure — from perfect competition to monopoly — shapes prices and power.', 5, 1),
  ('economics/global-economy/capital-flows-and-the-fx-market', 'economics', 'economics/global-economy', 'Capital Flows and the FX Market', 'capital-flows-and-the-fx-market', 'How money moves between countries, and how currencies are exchanged in the world''s largest market.', 2, 1),
  ('economics/global-economy/exchange-rate-calculations', 'economics', 'economics/global-economy', 'Exchange Rate Calculations', 'exchange-rate-calculations', 'How exchange rates are quoted, and how to compute cross rates and currency returns.', 3, 1),
  ('economics/global-economy/international-trade', 'economics', 'economics/global-economy', 'International Trade', 'international-trade', 'Why countries trade, who gains, and how comparative advantage shapes the flow of goods across borders.', 0, 1),
  ('economics/global-economy/introduction-to-geopolitics', 'economics', 'economics/global-economy', 'Introduction to Geopolitics', 'introduction-to-geopolitics', 'How cooperation and rivalry between states shape trade, capital, and markets.', 4, 1),
  ('economics/global-economy/trade-restrictions-and-blocs', 'economics', 'economics/global-economy', 'trade restrictions & blocs', 'trade-restrictions-and-blocs', '', 1, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/adam-smith-and-the-birth-of-classical-economics', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Adam Smith and the Birth of Classical Economics', 'adam-smith-and-the-birth-of-classical-economics', 'Adam Smith''s 1776 Wealth of Nations: the division of labor, the role of self-interest, and the ''invisible hand'' by which individual choices coordinate, unplanned, into shared prosperity.', 4, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/alfred-marshall-and-neoclassical-economics', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Alfred Marshall and Neoclassical Economics', 'alfred-marshall-and-neoclassical-economics', 'Marshall''s 1890 Principles, where supply and demand became the two blades of a scissors and the modern tools of partial equilibrium, elasticity, and marginal analysis took shape.', 9, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/ancient-and-medieval-economic-thought', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Ancient and Medieval Economic Thought', 'ancient-and-medieval-economic-thought', 'How Aristotle, the Scholastics, and other pre-modern thinkers reasoned about value, money, the ''just price,'' and the ethics of trade and lending — long before economics was a discipline of its own.', 0, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/david-ricardo-and-comparative-advantage', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'David Ricardo and Comparative Advantage', 'david-ricardo-and-comparative-advantage', 'Ricardo''s theories of rent, the labor theory of value, and comparative advantage — still the central argument for why nations gain from trade even when one can produce everything more cheaply.', 5, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/karl-marx-and-political-economy', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Karl Marx and Political Economy', 'karl-marx-and-political-economy', 'Marx''s critique of capitalism in Das Kapital: the labor theory of value, surplus value and exploitation, class conflict, and the crises he argued were built into the system.', 7, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/keynes-and-the-keynesian-revolution', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Keynes and the Keynesian Revolution', 'keynes-and-the-keynesian-revolution', 'Keynes''s 1936 General Theory, forged in the Great Depression: how shortfalls in aggregate demand cause mass unemployment, and the case for active fiscal and monetary policy.', 11, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/mercantilism-and-the-age-of-trade', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Mercantilism and the Age of Trade', 'mercantilism-and-the-age-of-trade', 'The 16th- to 18th-century doctrine that a nation''s wealth lay in its hoard of gold and silver, pursued through trade surpluses, protective tariffs, colonies, and state power.', 1, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/modern-schools-of-thought', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Modern Schools of Thought', 'modern-schools-of-thought', 'From rational expectations and new classical models to new Keynesian economics — how the discipline splintered and re-synthesized in the decades after the 1970s.', 13, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/monetarism-and-milton-friedman', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Monetarism and Milton Friedman', 'monetarism-and-milton-friedman', 'Friedman and the Chicago school''s counter-revolution — the money supply as the prime mover of inflation and output, and a sharp challenge to Keynesian demand management.', 12, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/the-austrian-school', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'The Austrian School', 'the-austrian-school', 'Menger, Mises, and Hayek on subjective value, the market as a process for discovering and using dispersed knowledge, and the monetary roots of the business cycle.', 10, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/the-history-of-money', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'The History of Money*', 'the-history-of-money', 'Why money exists and how it evolved: the barter economy and its frictions (the double coincidence of wants, indivisibility, perishability, and the lack of a common measure of value); money as a medium of exchange, unit of account, and store of value; commodity money and the gold standard; goldsmiths, promissory notes, and the birth of paper money; fractional reserve banking and money creation; and the modern age of central banks and fiat money.', 2, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/the-marginal-revolution', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'The Marginal Revolution', 'the-marginal-revolution', 'The 1870s breakthrough of Jevons, Menger, and Walras — value springs not from labor but from marginal utility, the worth of one more unit — recasting economics around subjective choice.', 8, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/the-physiocrats', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'The Physiocrats', 'the-physiocrats', 'The 18th-century French school of Quesnay and Turgot, who held that land and agriculture were the true source of wealth, mapped the economy in the Tableau Économique, and gave us the phrase laissez-faire.', 3, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/the-rise-of-behavioral-economics', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'The Rise of Behavioral Economics', 'the-rise-of-behavioral-economics', 'How Kahneman, Tversky, and later Thaler folded psychology back into economics, replacing the perfectly rational agent with a more human, boundedly rational one.', 14, 1),
  ('economics/history-of-economics/thomas-malthus-and-the-population-question', 'economics', 'economics/history-of-economics', 'Thomas Malthus and the Population Question', 'thomas-malthus-and-the-population-question', 'Malthus''s warning that population tends to outrun the food supply, how it helped earn economics the label ''the dismal science,'' and how the grim prediction actually fared.', 6, 1),
  ('economics/introduction/interest-rates', 'economics', 'economics/introduction', 'Interest Rates*', 'interest-rates', 'The price that links money today to money in the future — read as a required return, a discount rate, or an opportunity cost, and built from a real risk-free rate plus premiums for inflation, default, liquidity, and maturity risk.', 0, 1),
  ('economics/introduction/rates-of-return', 'economics', 'economics/introduction', 'Rates of Return*', 'rates-of-return', 'What an investment actually earns — income plus price change — and how to measure it: holding-period return, the arithmetic, geometric, and harmonic means, time- versus money-weighted return, and what''s left after fees, taxes, inflation, and leverage.', 1, 1),
  ('economics/macroeconomics/aggregate-output-prices-and-economic-growth', 'economics', 'economics/macroeconomics', 'Aggregate Output, Prices, and Economic Growth', 'aggregate-output-prices-and-economic-growth', 'The big-picture measures and forces of a national economy — what it produces, the overall price level, and what makes it grow over time.', 0, 1),
