  ('sociology-and-anthropology/sociological-theory/french-social-thought', 'sociology-and-anthropology', 'sociology-and-anthropology/sociological-theory', 'French Social Thought', 'french-social-thought', 'The French lineage that remade the human sciences: Comte''s invention of ''sociology''; Durkheim, the Année sociologique, and social facts; Mauss''s The Gift; structuralism — from Saussure''s linguistics to Lévi-Strauss''s kinship and myth, Barthes''s mythologies; the post-structuralist explosion — Foucault''s power/knowledge and discipline, Derrida''s deconstruction, Deleuze; Bourdieu — habitus, field, cultural capital, Distinction; Beauvoir and French feminism (Irigaray, Kristeva, Wittig); Latour, actor-network theory, and science studies; and the trans-Atlantic career of it all — how ''French Theory'' (Cusset) conquered and divided the American academy.', 1, 1),
